{"seq":33,"at":"2026-10-22","kind":"printed","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w24734"},"reason":"Printed on publish-or-perish card pp-050, category 2; the card's own words are kept in cardText — \"[Physiology and Anatomy] Why does color blindness affect males more than females?\nA. Because males have one less X chromosome\nB. Because of excessive testosterone\nC. Due to a lack of estrogen\nAnswer: A. The genes responsible for the most common forms of color blindness are on the X chromosome. Males have only one X chromosome, so a single defective gene can cause color blindness, whereas females have two, providing a backup if one is defective.\".","by":"merge art/architecture, art/design, art/painting, art/sculpture, belief/philosophy, belief/religion, belief/symbols, ear","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/publish-or-perish/pp-050.json","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"On which chromosome lie the genes for the most common forms of colour blindness, which is why it affects far more males than females?"},{"field":"de","new":"Auf welchem Chromosom liegen die Gene der häufigsten Formen der Farbenblindheit, weshalb sie weit mehr Männer als Frauen betrifft?"},{"field":"origin","new":"printed"},{"field":"printed","new":{"source":"publish-or-perish","card":"pp-050","category":2}},{"field":"cardText","diff":[["+","[Physiology and Anatomy] Why does color blindness affect males more than females?\nA. Because males have one less X chromosome\nB. Because of excessive testosterone\nC. Due to a lack of estrogen\nAnswer: A. The genes responsible for the most common forms of color blindness are on the X chromosome. Males have only one X chromosome, so a single defective gene can cause color blindness, whereas females have two, providing a backup if one is defective."]]},{"field":"fact","new":"f10181"}],"hash":"f9a5490ae194"},
